  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nAfter the aforementioned cool start, lower elevations will see \nanother dry, sub-90 degree day on Monday. Winds will pick up\nacross SE Oregon and the Snake Plain of Idaho as westerly flow\naloft mixes to the surface. The upper trough providing the \ncooler, breezy conditions will slide east of the area Tuesday, \nallowing for warm temperatures to return. By Wednesday highs are\nback into the mid-upper 90s across lower elevations (smoke \ncoverage/density dependent). There is no chance for\nprecipitation next week as monsoon moisture remains bottled up \nover the Four Corners. The hot and dry conditions will be\nfavorable for fire growth so smoke is likely to increase in\ncoverage and density.",
